{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n\n    >>> largest_divisor(15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # Per design context and test cases, for n=1, the largest divisor smaller than n is considered 1.\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Iterate downwards from n-1 to 1. The first number that divides n evenly is the largest.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return i"}
